{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792489769,"nonce":"abvEyUxarjLBHLVNBrQOR2TVOok=","message":"Reproduced before the producer fix with new emitted-data and offscreen pixel regressions. Three of the original five CPU cases failed: a 0.5 group emitted child alpha 0.5 instead of 1; nested zero-opacity groups destroyed child alpha; returning from dynamic/composite emission still baked group alpha into background children. Both new GPU cases failed: a half-opacity red child over blue produced [64,0,191,255] on the MSAA overlay route instead of [128,0,127,255]; the legacy clear route also multiplied premultiplied RGB again and produced [32,0,191,255]. The same scenes pass after keeping group alpha out of background primitive colours.\n\nGroup opacity is no longer stored on the explicit opacity stack. Primitive emission in the background batch uses explicit opacity only. current_opacity still reports the effective explicit/group product for callers and late image draws. Dynamic, composite scratch and foreground primitives still flatten group opacity because their independent dispatch paths do not process the background command ranges. This preserves the prior routing contract while fixing duplicate opacity where the group is actually composited. Layer pop continues restoring explicit scopes by their captured depths, without division, so zero-opacity groups work.\n\nReview caught a necessary companion: PrimitiveBatch::has_layer_effects and effect_layer_indices omitted opacity-only and 3D groups despite render_with_clear already processing them. The former omission could send a pure-opacity background group through z-layer splitting without its commands; the latter could redraw those children in a later z overlay. Both helpers now use the renderer's compositing criteria. A regression asserts exact exclusion of grouped indices while ungrouped z-layer siblings remain eligible.\n\nNative pixel coverage uses producer-created rectangles and filled paths with overlapping children, single/nested groups, explicit child opacity, zero group opacity and post-group state restoration. Single groups are checked through render_with_clear, render_overlay, and render_overlay_msaa at sample counts 1 and 4. Nested explicit-opacity coverage uses the ordered MSAA entry point. The separate legacy clear/overlay nested-composition and premultiplied-alpha implementations are not redesigned here; no claim is made that every legacy nested/effect route is correct.\n\nCross-batch group isolation remains a separate issue, e0a7502. It needs coordinated command ownership, range/animation-index changes and dispatch, not unconditional removal of flattened alpha. The originally observed z-layer bypass for a full background opacity-only group is fixed in this slice by the batch predicates; the follow-up concerns groups split across independent streams. Browser/mobile GPU pixels and timing are unverified. Full final validation results and the commit will follow.","files":null}]}